\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Christ, of all my hopes the ground,
\par Christ, the spring of all my joy,
\par Still in Thee may I be found,
\par Still for Thee my powers employ.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Let Thy love my heart inflame,
\par Keep Thy fear before my sight,
\par Be Thy praise my highest aim,
\par Be Thy smile my chief delight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When affliction clouds my sky,
\par And the wintry tempests blow,
\par Let Thy mercy-beaming eye
\par Sweetly cheer the night of woe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. When new triumphs of Thy name
\par Swell the raptured songs above,
\par May I feel a kindred flame,
\par Full of zeal, and full of love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Life's best joy, to see Thy praise
\par Fly on wings of gospel light,
\par Leading on millennial days,
\par Scattering all the shades of night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Fountain of o'erflowing grace,
\par Freely from Thy fullness give;
\par Till I close my earthly race,
\par May I prove it Christ to live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Firmly trusting in Thy blood,
\par Nothing shall my heart confound;
\par Safely shall  I pass the flood,
\par Safely reach Immanuel's ground.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Thus, O thus, an entrance give
\par To the land of cloudness sky;
\par Having known it Christ to live,
\par Let me find it gain to die.
\par                                  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

